<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — Refresh materialized remote content

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The <folio:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; <folio:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn"
                  id="Definitions_RefreshMaterialized"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">

  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_RefreshMaterialized">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_RefreshMaterialized" name="Refresh materialized remote content" processRef="Process_RefreshMaterialized" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_RefreshMaterialized" name="Refresh materialized remote content" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Owner, 2026-09-20: &quot;also need to know about refreshing amterialed remote content. general process used everywhere.&quot;

REFRESH IS NOT RE-IMPORT, and the difference is the whole diagram. It needs three answers, not one: what changed upstream, what changed locally since, and what to do when BOTH did. upstream-pins.json answers the first for one caller and nothing answers the other two anywhere.

An ARCHIVAL copy is not refreshed. Re-fetching it would defeat it: the copy exists to survive the source, so replacing it with whatever the source says today discards exactly the state it was keeping. What an archive gets instead is a FIXITY CHECK — has our copy rotted — which is a different question with a different remedy.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <folio:policy enforcement="strict" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="Process_RefreshMaterialized_LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_0" name="Contributor (human or agent)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Reached only when both upstream and local changed, which is the one case this process refuses to resolve by rule: which side wins depends on why the local edit was made, a fact only this lane has.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_Due</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Adjudicate</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_1" name="Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Runs whichever of the two paths Gateway_Purpose selects. On the working path it answers the two comparisons — upstream and local — whose combination Gateway_Both reads to decide whether a human must adjudicate; on the archival path it never compares to the source at all, since fixity asks only whether the copy itself rotted.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Purpose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Fixity</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Upstream</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Local</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Both</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_2" name="Corpus — L1 source knowledge graph">
        <bpmn:documentation>Where the refreshed content actually lands, and the one place the five import gates are re-asked rather than inherited — a licence can change since the original import, and a collection can grow past a size somebody already agreed to, so passing the gates once is never treated as passing them for good.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Apply</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_Fresh</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_Due" name="A copy is due
for re-check">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Purpose" name="working,
or archival?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Fixity" name="ARCHIVAL
verify fixity —
never re-fetch">
      <bpmn:documentation>Re-compute the digest and compare. An archive is NEVER re-fetched — the source is what it exists to survive, so replacing it with today's version discards the state it was keeping. A mismatch means OUR copy rotted, and the remedy is restoration from a backup, not re-download.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="materialize-remote" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Upstream" name="WORKING
what changed upstream">
      <bpmn:documentation>Compare the recorded upstreamVersion against the source. `could not reach the source` is a THIRD answer and is never reported as `unchanged` — an unreachable source is the sourceLoss gate firing late.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="materialize-remote" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Local" name="What changed LOCALLY
since">
      <bpmn:documentation>The half nothing answers today. A materialized copy that was edited in place is not a copy any more, and overwriting it silently destroys work whose existence the process never established.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="materialize-remote" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Both" name="Both changed?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_Adjudicate" name="Adjudicate the conflict">
      <bpmn:documentation>A human or agentic decision, never a merge rule. Which side wins depends on why the local edit was made, and a process that picked automatically would be choosing without the one fact that decides it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="materialize-remote" />
        <folio:skill ref="adjudication" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Apply" name="Re-materialize, re-asking
the five gates">
      <bpmn:documentation>The gates are re-asked, not inherited: a licence can change, and a collection can grow past the size a caller agreed to.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="materialize-remote" />
        <folio:bean op="note" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Fresh" name="Fresh, and the graph
records against what">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_10</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="StartEvent_Due" targetRef="Gateway_Purpose" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" name="archival" sourceRef="Gateway_Purpose" targetRef="Task_Fixity" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" name="working" sourceRef="Gateway_Purpose" targetRef="Task_Upstream" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="Task_Upstream" targetRef="Task_Local" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="Task_Local" targetRef="Gateway_Both" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" name="yes" sourceRef="Gateway_Both" targetRef="Task_Adjudicate" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_7" name="no" sourceRef="Gateway_Both" targetRef="Task_Apply" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_8" sourceRef="Task_Adjudicate" targetRef="Task_Apply" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_9" sourceRef="Task_Fixity" targetRef="EndEvent_Fresh" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_10" sourceRef="Task_Apply" targetRef="EndEvent_Fresh" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_RefreshMaterialized">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_RefreshMaterialized" bpmnElement="Collaboration_RefreshMaterialized">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_RefreshMaterialized_di" bpmnElement="Participant_RefreshMaterialized" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="130" y="60" width="2010" height="610" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_0_di" bpmnElement="Lane_0" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="60" width="1980" height="190" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_1_di" bpmnElement="Lane_1" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1980" height="190" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_2_di" bpmnElement="Lane_2" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="440" width="1980" height="190" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_Due_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_Due">
        <dc:Bounds x="200" y="127" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="160" y="168" width="116" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Purpose_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Purpose">
        <dc:Bounds x="450" y="310" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="410" y="365" width="130" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Fixity_di" bpmnElement="Task_Fixity">
        <dc:Bounds x="700" y="410" width="190" height="100" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Upstream_di" bpmnElement="Task_Upstream">
        <dc:Bounds x="700" y="285" width="190" height="100" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Local_di" bpmnElement="Task_Local">
        <dc:Bounds x="950" y="285" width="190" height="100" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Both_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Both">
        <dc:Bounds x="1200" y="310" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1160" y="365" width="130" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Adjudicate_di" bpmnElement="Task_Adjudicate">
        <dc:Bounds x="1450" y="220" width="190" height="100" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Apply_di" bpmnElement="Task_Apply">
        <dc:Bounds x="1450" y="475" width="190" height="100" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_Fresh_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_Fresh">
        <dc:Bounds x="1700" y="507" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1660" y="548" width="116" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
        <di:waypoint x="218" y="163" />
        <di:waypoint x="218" y="335" />
        <di:waypoint x="450" y="335" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
        <di:waypoint x="500" y="335" />
        <di:waypoint x="700" y="460" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="565" y="305" width="90" height="26" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_3">
        <di:waypoint x="500" y="335" />
        <di:waypoint x="700" y="335" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="565" y="305" width="90" height="26" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_4">
        <di:waypoint x="890" y="335" />
        <di:waypoint x="950" y="335" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_5">
        <di:waypoint x="1140" y="335" />
        <di:waypoint x="1200" y="335" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_6">
        <di:waypoint x="1225" y="360" />
        <di:waypoint x="1225" y="270" />
        <di:waypoint x="1450" y="270" />
